WEBVTT

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:18.780
Final spurt!

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:38.930
Yes!

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:43.270
We got official records!

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:44.540
Yeah!

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:26.000
<b><i>Run with the Wind</i></b>

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.710
<b>Tsuru-no-yu</b>

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:32.130
Hot! It's hot!

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:33.590
Please stop doing that!

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:36.180
Hey! Hey!

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:39.270
Please stop!

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:42.710
We'll get in trouble if we make too much noise!

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:42.710
Everyone's unique.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.540
Naturally, so are runners.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:49.670
Some are better at running
on the track than on roads.

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:54.050
Some go for sprints while others
excel at managing their pace.

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:57.150
Uphill, downhill. Everyone's
good at something different.

00:02:57.970 --> 00:03:00.350
So we shouldn't worry about it?

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:03.560
Uniqueness certainly sounds nice,

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:07.680
but doesn't that mean some people
aren't suited to running at all?

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.370
I'm worried.

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:14.380
Times aren't everything.

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:17.370
But isn't that our goal?

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:22.180
We need official records
to run in the Hakone qualifier.

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:24.890
But as long as you feel it's working—

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:28.170
But we're amateurs.

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:34.090
Unless you tell us what's working,
we won't know what is.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:40.560
True to its name, long distance running
is a battle of endurance.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:43.260
It's not easy to compare results.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:49.500
Sorry, but I'm at my limit.

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:54.500
I meant with the water.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:58.500
<b><i>Overflowing Drops</i></b>

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:05.110
Can we even run in this?

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:07.770
They're not very breatheable,
but we don't have a choice.

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:11.420
Some of you weren't wearing
clothing suitable for rain.

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:15.440
We should get proper matching ones already.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:17.920
It can't be helped. This is temporary.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:19.560
Let's go.

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:26.550
Sorry, Nira. You need to stay home today.

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:36.100
So hot.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.830
It's so stuffy, this is no different
from getting rained on.

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:41.170
Let's imagine that's the point of this practice.

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:48.800
I feel like I just came back from the pool.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:50.890
I know what you mean. I'm exhausted.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:54.600
If you don't dry off, you'll catch a cold.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:57.190
Should we count this as showering today?

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:58.640
Yeah, let's.

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:01.070
Please go back to your own room!

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:03.920
Our room leaks when it rains.

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:06.070
I've got first period,
so I'll see you guys later.

00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:07.460
See ya.

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:08.380
See you later.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:15.340
Shindo never skips class.

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:17.420
Is he okay?

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:18.610
What?

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:22.560
He seemed pretty depressed
after yesterday's meet.

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:23.970
And he's so earnest.

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:28.030
But he has a girlfriend, right?

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:29.970
Hey, that's right.

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:31.890
Who cares, then? He's totally fine.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:36.320
He's so busy. When does
he get to see his girlfriend?

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:38.040
Maybe at school.

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:40.730
<b>Kansei University</b>

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:40.730
What? You've seen his girlfriend?

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:42.410
Not a single time.

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:45.290
I don't think anyone's seen her yet.

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:50.350
Maybe Shindo pushed himself so hard...

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.660
That he imagined a girlfriend
who doesn't exist...

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:55.520
Hey, were you waiting long? Sorry.

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:58.080
Come on! Don't sulk.

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:03.390
Yikes!

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:14.680
<b>Monthly Track and Field Report</b>

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:20.650
<b>Acupuncture/Massage</b>

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:20.650
<b>Iimura Chiropractic Clinic</b>

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:22.010
You're protecting the opposite side.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:26.290
I've been trying to be conscious of it.

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:28.860
Well, once something breaks,

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:31.780
you've got no choice except
to take your time fixing it.

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:33.780
Yes, sir.

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:49.260
<b>Monthly Track and Field Report</b>

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:51.570
Damn that Fujioka.

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:55.180
<b>Field Closed Due to Rain</b>

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:01.240
Nope. It's closed today.

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:04.840
Should we use the field?
We can focus on just cross country today.

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:06.140
No way.

00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:08.930
The mud makes it too hard
to run. I'm against it.

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:11.330
You just don't want to get dirty.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:12.670
What should we do?

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:14.850
Let's run on the roads.

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:17.040
We just need to watch out for cars.

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:20.720
Yeah. We'll choose the safests course we can.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:25.960
Let's get this over with 
so we can go to Tsuru-no-yu.

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:29.630
Nice.

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:33.360
Can't we at least use the club
budget to buy rain coats?

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:35.850
We should be using it in some meaningful way.

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:38.290
They're supposed to be our fan club.

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:41.560
We still only have fifteen members.

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:43.770
That's all?

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:47.290
We still don't have enough
to buy matching track uniforms.

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:51.400
We have the support of
everyone at the shopping center,

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:52.990
but we need a little more.

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:56.750
If only the Trans America Quiz was still on.

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:58.950
I'd win us some prize money.

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:03.170
Perhaps we could win some kind of tournament.

00:08:03.410 --> 00:08:06.770
After all, we haven't achieved anything.

00:08:06.770 --> 00:08:08.400
You're right.

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:11.650
Isn't there some kind of 
national event we could run in?

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:15.140
There is one.

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:17.100
What's it called?

00:08:18.170 --> 00:08:19.350
The Inter-College.

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:23.990
The All-Japan Intercollegiate Championship.

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:27.270
<b>Kanto Track and Field 
Intercollegiate Championship</b>

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:26.740
Look, I found it.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:31.530
Huh. The Kanto meet was in May.

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:35.310
Did you read Fujioka's article?

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:36.410
I happen to have.

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:42.180
There were some curious things written in it.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:50.710
<b>Fujioka Kazuma Runner Interview
</b>Boulder of a Race

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:46.770
I ran the race I wanted this time,

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:50.270
but there are more strong
runners hiding in Kanto.

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:54.980
I believe they'll be ready by 
the time Ekiden season rolls around.

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:58.180
I'll make sure not to 
underestimate them as I wait.

00:09:00.020 --> 00:09:00.990
Kakeru,

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:05.800
do you know what the greatest compliment
you can give a long distance runner is?

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:08.510
Is it to call him fast?

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:09.400
No.

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:12.610
It's to call him strong.

00:09:14.980 --> 00:09:16.190
Strong?

00:09:30.950 --> 00:09:34.620
You can't survive long
distances on speed alone.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:39.040
You hold out through difficult phases
to keep on moving your body forward.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:43.870
Every day, you have to push
yourself a little harder in practice.

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:47.940
What long distance runners need is strength.

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:55.190
Fujioka is strong, both
as a runner and as a captain.

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:58.440
But Fujioka is Fujioka.

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:04.270
I regret that we weren't able to show
him your abilities at the Inter-College,

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:06.340
but there's no need to panic.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:08.850
Believe in yourself.

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:11.090
It takes time to become stronger.

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:16.480
Fujioka's on your mind, too.

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:23.500
I understand what you're trying to say,
but why are you telling me this now?

00:10:25.420 --> 00:10:26.780
Are you anxious?

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:28.390
Anxious?

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:32.860
5000m Best Times

00:10:28.870 --> 00:10:32.320
Half of our members still haven't
achieved an official record.

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:37.400
Shindo and Yuki haven't
improved much in a month,

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:40.450
despite practicing so hard.

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:43.190
Is that why?

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:50.500
When Prince's time improved,
I felt like I understood running a little.

00:10:51.990 --> 00:10:54.710
But it's still difficult.

00:10:55.700 --> 00:10:58.470
Honestly, I'm anxious.

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:13.360
How's this?

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:15.350
Well...

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:17.950
Could you make this part easier to read?

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:18.860
Got it.

00:11:19.730 --> 00:11:21.930
A website, huh?

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:27.330
We're going to make it so people who live
far away can sign up for the fan club.

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:30.790
We'll never get anywhere just waiting.

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:33.120
And you've got seminars tomorrow, too.

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:35.940
You're truly amazing, Shindo.

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:40.630
What? But you passed the bar exam in one try.

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:42.180
Well, yeah.

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:43.360
I'm going to bed.

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:46.170
Wake me up if there's
anything you don't understand.

00:11:46.170 --> 00:11:47.760
Thank you.

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:49.980
Please don't push yourself too hard.

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:53.440
I'm okay, Musa. Good night.

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:13.250
Chikusei-so

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:21.880
Sorry, I'm late. Sorry.

00:12:27.820 --> 00:12:28.580
What?

00:12:29.940 --> 00:12:31.050
Sorry.

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:35.420
After all, it seems like there's something you'd
rather be spending your time on than me.

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:37.790
That's not true.

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:38.820
There is, isn't there?

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:41.180
There is.

00:12:43.180 --> 00:12:45.640
So I thought we should break up.

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:53.870
Final spurt!

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:55.860
You can do it!

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:05.380
That's enough for today. Cool down, everyone.

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:06.320
Excuse me!

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:12.350
Could I run one more?

00:13:15.570 --> 00:13:16.690
Just one more.

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:18.830
Please!

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:22.940
Your lap time is increasing. You shouldn't—

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:26.000
Times aren't everything.
Isn't that what you said?

00:13:27.460 --> 00:13:29.770
It's true that I want to improve my times,

00:13:29.770 --> 00:13:33.160
but more than that,
I just want to run right now!

00:13:33.490 --> 00:13:36.870
Just until I'm satisfied. That's all!

00:13:39.690 --> 00:13:40.930
Please!

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:43.800
Please!

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:56.540
Me, too.

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:57.560
What?

00:13:57.560 --> 00:14:01.260
I was just feeling like I could
run some more today, too.

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:06.100
Fine, then.

00:14:06.100 --> 00:14:07.110
Me, too.

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:14.830
You're all a bunch of freaks.

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:15.970
Me, too.

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:18.540
I'll record their times.

00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:30.470
<b>Bond</b>

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:32.670
I feel the same way.

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:36.190
I want to run more.

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:39.440
Even though I've been told
not to run, I'm running.

00:14:41.970 --> 00:14:47.930
Maybe I'd forgotten to listen to my feelings.

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:56.540
Ready, go!

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:14.340
Shindo, the way you run's a little different.

00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:15.060
What?

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:19.140
I watched your last lap from behind you.

00:15:19.760 --> 00:15:24.750
Your center of gravity or whatever
is different from the other guys.

00:15:25.220 --> 00:15:28.940
Especially from guys 
who speed ahead like Kakeru.

00:15:29.430 --> 00:15:30.540
Really?

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:33.910
I guess everyone does run differently.

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:35.490
It's the first time I'd noticed.

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:39.200
Imagine raising your center
of gravity a little higher.

00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:41.670
Don't curve your chest.

00:15:42.610 --> 00:15:44.380
You could be doing this outside.

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:45.740
That's rich coming from you.

00:15:47.700 --> 00:15:50.710
Thanks. Would you be willing to help me again?

00:15:50.710 --> 00:15:51.690
Of course.

00:15:51.690 --> 00:15:52.640
You, too.

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:56.390
I was just telling you what I noticed.

00:15:57.630 --> 00:15:59.560
You're doing something after this?

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:02.310
I wanted to finish the website today.

00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:05.770
I'll make some tea.

00:16:08.470 --> 00:16:11.390
He's starting to become a little sociable.

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:15.660
I've been wondering for a while now.

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:17.980
Is this your home?

00:16:17.980 --> 00:16:18.740
Yeah.

00:16:20.260 --> 00:16:22.560
What kind of secluded region
does your family live in?

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:24.900
We have roads, you know.

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:29.940
There are roads, but it's faster
to climb the valley to get to school.

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:31.950
Your parents wouldn't drive you?

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:35.040
My family runs a farm, so they're busy in the mornings.

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:37.220
If anything, they needed my help.

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:42.230
If I had a daughter, I'd definitely
make her marry you.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:43.710
What does that mean?

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:46.310
You've got your shit together.

00:16:47.390 --> 00:16:49.730
I don't. Not at all.

00:16:50.350 --> 00:16:55.840
Shindo, you were the first one
to say you wanted to run.

00:16:56.610 --> 00:16:57.820
Is that right?

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:04.210
I'm sorry. I was so sure then that you'd give up.

00:17:04.650 --> 00:17:06.060
Well, you know...

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:08.690
But I was wrong.

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:12.930
This team never would've formed without you,

00:17:12.930 --> 00:17:15.930
and it can't keep going without you.

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:19.330
You're strong, Shindo.

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:25.690
Kansei University Track and Field Team

00:17:20.690 --> 00:17:23.360
The ten of us will run in the Hakone Ekiden.

00:17:23.800 --> 00:17:25.690
It's nice to dream.

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:29.570
But anyone can just talk about their dreams.

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:33.650
I'm not about that.
Neither is anyone else, right?

00:17:34.590 --> 00:17:36.110
If you say you'll do it, do it.

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:38.060
Haiji's the same way.

00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:42.610
I'm not strong.

00:17:42.610 --> 00:17:45.290
I just do what needs
to be done, no matter what.

00:17:47.260 --> 00:17:48.240
Yes.

00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:52.000
You'll definitely get that official record.

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:56.010
This again? But you're normally so cool.

00:17:56.010 --> 00:17:58.460
Shut up. I said you'll get it.

00:17:58.460 --> 00:18:01.230
Everything I've said would
happen has happened.

00:18:01.230 --> 00:18:03.470
Then I'll trust you.

00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:05.680
What's that?

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:07.430
Nothing.

00:18:07.430 --> 00:18:10.550
Man, working at night isn't good for my eyes!

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:12.070
Seriously?

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:41.380
Shindo. Shindo!

00:18:46.570 --> 00:18:49.530
Shindo, it's morning.

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:52.020
<b>Member Profiles</b>

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:52.020
<b>Kiyose Haiji  Iwakura Yukihiko  Sakaguchi Yohei  Hirata Akihiko  Sugiyama Takashi</b>

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:52.020
<b>Kashiwazaki Akane  Musa Kamura  Jo Taro  Jo Jiro  Kuraha ra Kakeru</b>

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:54.480
<b>I'm an Ekiden fan. I saw your website! 
Please practice hard in preparation 
for the Hakone Ekiden! 
You have my support!</b>

00:18:53.410 --> 00:18:54.480
We got one!

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:56.150
We got one, Shindo!

00:18:57.650 --> 00:18:58.520
What?

00:18:58.520 --> 00:19:01.610
Yuki, Kakeru! Look at this!

00:19:01.610 --> 00:19:03.950
What? Let me sleep.

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:06.370
<b>Yaokatsu</b>

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:10.330
Kansei University Track and Field Team

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:10.350
I doubt you'd be able to meet them
even if you went to the university.

00:19:10.910 --> 00:19:14.340
Hey, Hanako. Could you run over to Aotake and—

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:16.390
We're running in the Tokyo Sports Uni meet!

00:19:16.390 --> 00:19:18.340
Please come out to support us!

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:19.960
Please!

00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:23.380
We're running in the Tokyo Sports Uni meet!

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:25.840
Please come out to support us!

00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:27.290
Here they come.

00:19:27.290 --> 00:19:30.190
That's the Kansei Uni Track and Field Team.

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:32.260
Hey!

00:19:33.140 --> 00:19:34.990
It's Hana!

00:19:34.990 --> 00:19:36.380
Come with us, Hana!

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:37.610
Run with us!

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:39.900
Okay. I'll follow you on my bike.

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:53.710
<b>Tokyo Sport University</b>

00:20:03.350 --> 00:20:05.010
The mountains of Hakone are?

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:07.720
The steepest in the world! Yeah!

